  "footnote": "Sources: CAPA and Dengta Pro (Apr 2025, Dengta platform data), CAPA live music report (DoNews, Apr 2026)",
  "notes": "Who comes. In 2024, 66.1% of large-concert audiences were women and 74.9% were aged 18 to 34, adding 25.8% aged 18 to 24, 31.1% aged 25 to 29 and 18.0% aged 30 to 34. Festival crowds are younger still: 84.9% aged 18 to 34, 67.1% women. In 2025, people born in 2000 or later made up 32.5% of the live music audience. That is exactly who a young drinks brand wants. But the market is not the show. Household-name singers pull the age up: 44.5% of Dao Lang's 2024 tour audience was 50 or older, against 20.3% for Wakin Chau and 10.7% for Andy Lau. So we choose shows by the artist's own audience profile, not by the market average. That is our first test for any artist: their audience overlaps with 18 to 34. Then many tour dates, no public controversy, and acceptance of a morals clause. The profile data come from the Dengta platform, so they are effectively company figures."
